MID_SCXX_00_01_m01: <EDH>
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_001: Haaah... Haaah... Well, we got out of the dungeon...\nsomehow.
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_002: Ughhh... Can't believe you'd be so reckless, taking\nadvantage of the bandits' commotion to bust me out.
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_003: Seems like recklessness runs in the family. But rest\nassured, we do have a plan.
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_004: Are there no pursuers? I had hoped to find someone\nskilled to fight.
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_005: Is your father unharmed? We should quit this place\nforthwith.
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_006: Nicely done, Cai. Keep it up and this ought to\nbe easy.
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_008: 
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_009: 
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_010: Help is here, eh? Sorry to put you through this.
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_011: If things get hairy, just leave me. I'm long past ready\nfor death.
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_012: Not a chance, Castor. Cai and I are not letting\nthat happen.
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_013: Ultand and Peter stayed behind in the dungeon to\nkeep watch for us.
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_014: Ultand stayed behind in the dungeon to keep watch\nfor us.
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_015: Peter stayed behind in the dungeon to keep watch\nfor us.
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_016: For our part, we're pressing on, and we're keeping\nPop alive.
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_017: I expected little but boredom, but no...I scent\nstrength in this place.
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_018: Our path has gone unbarred thus far, but we should\nnot expect that to last.
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_019: The commotion underground's not exactly going to\ndie down—which ought to help us escape.
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_021: 
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_022: 
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_023: Who are you?! What are you doing here?!
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_024: Ah! Castor? What's going on?
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_025: Centurio... I...
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_026: This is bad. Tialla, take Pop and get out of here.
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_027: I will!
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_028: Cai, are you the one who broke him out?
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_029: I don't have a choice. It's either this, or they kill him.
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_030: A prisoner leaving their cell without permission is a\nserious breach of regulations.
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_031: I, Corundum Centurio, cannot overlook this.
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_032: Pop's life is more important than your stupid rules.\nYou're not taking him back!
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_033: We will apprehend the prisoner and eliminate\ncollaborators by force.
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_034: "Corundum," was it? Challenge accepted!
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_035: I had hoped to avoid battle, but I now see no\nalternative. Ready yourself, Cai.
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_036: Quite the threat. We can't exactly leave now,\ncan we?
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_038: 
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_039: 
MID_SCXX_00_01_m01_040: Right. We're stopping Centurio here and now.
MID_SCXX_00_02_m01: <TH>
MID_SCXX_00_02_m01_001: Cai... I will not hold anything back, even for you.
MID_SCXX_00_02_m01_002: I can tell you're determined, but so am I.
MID_SCXX_00_02_m02: <TH>
MID_SCXX_00_02_m02_001: At last, a worthy battle. Hm?
MID_SCXX_00_02_m02_002: Dietrich, I'm sorry I got you caught up in this. But\ndo not kill Centurio.
MID_SCXX_00_02_m02_003: Very well. I do not thirst for it.
MID_SCXX_00_02_m03: <TH>
MID_SCXX_00_02_m03_001: I'm sorry I got you caught up in this, Theodora, but—
MID_SCXX_00_02_m03_002: I know, and I agree that killing the vulkan would\ncause more problems than it solves.
MID_SCXX_00_02_m04: <TH>
MID_SCXX_00_02_m04_001: I know it's a lot to ask, Leda, but please don't\nkill Centurio.
MID_SCXX_00_02_m04_002: Heh, I would never! As long as he doesn't\ndo anything lethal either.
MID_SCXX_00_02_m06: <TH>
MID_SCXX_00_02_m06_001: I'm sorry for getting you mixed up in this, Orchel.\nBut about Centurio—
MID_SCXX_00_02_m06_002: Don't you worry, Cai. I always try to subdue foes\nrather than kill them, you see. 
MID_SCXX_00_02_m07: <TH>
MID_SCXX_00_02_m07_001: I know I'm asking a lot here, Anatolia, but please\ndon't kill Centurio.
MID_SCXX_00_02_m07_002: If that's what you wish, I'll make every effort not to.
MID_SCXX_00_02_m08: <TH>
MID_SCXX_00_02_m08_001: So you're not backing down. Exactly what does my\nfather mean to you?
MID_SCXX_00_02_m08_002: That question was answered long ago, when he\nturned his back on our friendship.
MID_SCXX_00_02_m09: <TH>
MID_SCXX_00_02_m09_001: Ultand! You were in a perfect position to stop Cai.
MID_SCXX_00_02_m09_002: Forgive me, Centurio. I'm doing this for Aurora.
MID_SCXX_00_02_m10: <TH>
MID_SCXX_00_02_m10_001: I-I don't like this, but I'm doing it for Cai.
MID_SCXX_00_02_m10_002: For Cai. Your...friend.
MID_SCXX_00_02_m11: <TH>
MID_SCXX_00_02_m11_001: Talimun! Even you are on their side?
MID_SCXX_00_02_m11_002: Don't get me wrong. I'm not doing this for the kid.\nI'm doing it for you, Centurio.
MID_SCXX_00_02_m12: <TH>
MID_SCXX_00_02_m12_001: No matter what you throw at me, I will not\nback down.
MID_SCXX_00_02_m13: <TH>
MID_SCXX_00_02_m13_001: Not yet... I... What was I even fighting for?
MID_SCXX_00_e01: <TH>
MID_SCXX_00_e01_001: Everyone! Over there! We must pursue Cast—\nI mean, the prisoner!
MID_SCXX_00_e01_002: Don't let Centurio or the others get over there! We'll\nlose Pop forever if {SetColor=Gold}any of them reach that location{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SCXX_00_e02: <TH>
MID_SCXX_00_e02_001: Here's what we've got to remember... Tialla set up\na {SetColor=Gold}sneaky tactic {SetColor=Default}with the {SetColor=Gold}censers{SetColor=Default} in these streets!
MID_SCXX_00_e03: <TH>
MID_SCXX_00_e03_001: I don't know what the tactic is, exactly...but\n{SetColor=Gold}destroying a censer{SetColor=Default} is the key. I'll give it a try!
MID_SCXX_00_e04: <TH>
MID_SCXX_00_e04_001: I'm...I'm going numb! This isn't only ashes!\nSomething else was in all that!
MID_SCXX_00_e04_002: Ha, classic Tialla! Let's put this to good use.
MID_SCXX_00_e08: <TH>
MID_SCXX_00_e08_001: No! The plan...failed...
MID_SCXX_00_e09: <TH>
MID_SCXX_00_e09_001: Our aim is to apprehend Castor. Remove anyone who\nstands in the way, and push forward.
MID_SCXX_00_e10: <TH>
MID_SCXX_00_e10_001: We should still be able to reach him. All soldiers, get\nthat prisoner! Hold nothing back!
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01: <EDH>
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_001: Urgh... Haaah... Haaah...
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_039: 
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_040: 
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_002: I'm so sorry, Centurio. Please stop fighting me.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_003: You appear bewildered. Cutting you down would not\nslake my thirst.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_004: Whatever mix of grievances you nurse, I suggest\nconceding if you value your life.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_005: If you like not getting killed, do as he says.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_007: 
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_008: 
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_009: I'm gravely wounded, there is no question. I could\nnot move even if I wanted to.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_010: There is no need to point out the obvious, Your\nMajesty. I could not move even if I wanted to.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_011: It appears Castor has escaped. Good for you, Cai.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_012: Ah?!
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_013: When Aurora and Castor ran away together, I was\nthe one who commanded the search party.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_014: My role in that—my decisions—have troubled me for\nquite some time.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_015: I knew they loved each other with all their hearts.\nBut I still chose rules and regulations over them.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_016: I took Aurora's infant son away from her as she wept\nand pleaded, and I returned her to her temple.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_017: I deserve no less than for you to raise your spear\nagainst me, Cai.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_018: I did wonder why I was allowed to stay with Pop\nuntil I'd grown up.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_019: You must have bargained with the temple for me.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_020: Even Corundum had to have some kind\nof conscience.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_021: Mmph. Go, Cai. I'll say that I sustained a deep\nwound and fell here.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_022: You took advantage of the opportunity and fled. I did\nnot see the faces of your collaborators. Understood?
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_023: Thank you.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_024: Ah. I'm glad that all worked out.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_025: Ohhh. My legs are still shaking.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_026: I want to thank you for looking out for my son.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_027: Looking out? For me? We rescued you!
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_028: Easy now. What matters is everything ended\nwell, alright?
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_029: Windstorm... Perhaps if we'd met sooner, we\ncould have had a fine duel.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_030: The important thing is that we extracted you safely.\nBe well.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_031: And yet my father had to... No, it's fine. I'll let this lie\nfor once.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_033: 
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_034: 
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_035: Thank you so much for helping me out. I want you to\nhave this.
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_037: We'll head back to Ribeira now. But you take\ncare, OK?
MID_SCXX_00_03_m01_038: If you ever need help, just call on me, and I'll\ncome running.